Explore automatic agent dispatch from ticket changes.

Consider a local process that watches ticket folders and starts an AI coding agent when a ticket
has a configured status and assignee, such as `status:ready` and `assignee:Clanker`.

The design should cover safe ticket claiming, duplicate event handling, agent concurrency, Git
branches or worktrees, failure states, logging, and configurable agent commands. A separate daemon
is preferred so this can work without Visual Studio Code.

Consider options for a normal daemon, but also a UI frontend for configuration and monitoring.

Work will need to be done on Git worktrees rather than branching off the main repo because
otherwise there is too much risk of having the state of the repo being pulled out from under me
or other agents. Also need to consider how the worktree is cleaned up - I would rather not have
to deal with that manually.

Something will need to be considered regarding the agent asking for permission to do stuff. It
should always be allowed to do things on it's own worktree, but never on the main repo. Not sure on
the safety of this however. Consider.